{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Under it.</b> In its place." "<b>A scar of the inflammation.</b> As the Targum renders: רֹשֶׁם שִׁחֲנָא — it is nothing but the mark of the inflammation visible in the flesh. Every צָרֶבֶת is a term for skin irritation caused by heat, as in ״וְנִצְרְבוּ בָהּ כָּל פָּנִים״ (Ezekiel 21); רייטרו״ר בְּלַעַז." "<b>A scar.</b> רייטרי״שמנט בְּלַעַז."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French retraiture, 'scar/mark left by a burn'", 2 "the la'az appears to be Old French retraitement or a related form meaning 'scar/treatment of a mark'; the Hebrew spelling is unusual"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:13.665085212Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}